TYPES.md §9.3, EVALUATION.md §2.1: of an entry key given in two files, the first is the one in (file path, position) order, whatever order the files were read in: x first in a/a.canon, y first in a/a/z.canon, which sorts before a/b.canon.
-- a/b.canon --
package a

entry rows.y { n: 3 }
-- a/a/z.canon --
package a

entry rows.y { n: 4 }

entry rows.x { n: 2 }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Row {
  n: Int
}

local let rows: table Row = {}

entry rows.x { n: 1 }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3101]  a/a/z.canon:5:12
  duplicate key x in rows (first at a/a.canon:9)

error[E3101]  a/b.canon:3:12
  duplicate key y in rows (first at a/a/z.canon:3)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
